  "worked_solution": "Let's rewrite our integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{7}{25-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{7}{25}\\int \\frac{1}{1-{(\\frac{x}{5})}^{2}}\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for the inverse hyperbolic tangent,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1-{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{artanh}\u2061u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{5})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{5}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{5}\\,\u27f9\\,\\text{d}x=5\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and compute it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{7}{25-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{7}{25}\\int \\frac{1}{1-{(\\frac{x}{5})}^{2}}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{25}\\int \\frac{1}{1-{u}^{2}}\\cdot 5\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{5}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{1-{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{5}\\operatorname{artanh}\u2061u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{5}\\operatorname{artanh}\u2061(\\frac{x}{5})+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that this result is subject to the condition $|\\frac{x}{5}|<1.$",
